            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "1",
          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">​</span><strong>Jugding</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>In the sentence, out of all the bold parts&nbsp;&#39;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Jugding</span>&#39;&nbsp;is the word that has no meaning.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>So, &#39;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Jugding</span>&#39; is incorrectly spelt word.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>The correct spelling is &#39;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Judging</span>&#39; which means&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">form an opinion or conclusion about.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Let us know the meanings of other words:\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li><strong>legality -&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">the quality or state of being in accordance with the law.</span></li>\n\t\t<li><strong>ordinance -&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">an authoritative order.</span></li>\n\t\t<li><strong>province -&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">a principal administrative division of a country or empire.</span><br />\n\t\t&nbsp;</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">So, the correct sentence is -&nbsp;</span><em>Judging the legality of the&nbsp;ordinance&nbsp;is within the province of the courts.</em></p>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
