          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">​</span><strong>luxrious</strong><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\"><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>In the sentence, out of all the bold parts&nbsp;&#39;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">luxrious</span>&#39;&nbsp;is the word that has no meaning.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>So, &#39;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">luxrious</span>&#39; is incorrectly spelt word.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>The correct spelling is &#39;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">luxurious</span>&#39; which means&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">extremely comfortable or elegant, especially when involving great expense.</span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Let us know the meanings of other words:\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li><strong>appearance -&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">the way that someone or something looks.</span></li>\n\t\t<li><strong>inhabitation -&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">the act of inhabiting&nbsp;</span>or&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">the state of being inhabited.</span></li>\n\t\t<li><strong>sentiment -&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);  \">a view or opinion that is held or expressed.</span><br />\n\t\t&nbsp;</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">So, the correct sentence is -&nbsp;</span><em>I don&#39;t long for&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">luxurious</span>&nbsp;life and gorgeous&nbsp;appearance, but I need a complete&nbsp;inhabitation&nbsp;for the&nbsp;sentiment.</em></p>",
